h2. 🔄 Daily App Refresh

⏰ Every day at 16:00 (Lisbon time) the app performs a refresh

⚠️ Recommendation
** ✅ Avoid running critical suites between 15:50–16:10 to reduce instability

h2. 🧪 How Gaia Tests Must Be Executed

✅ Gaia tests must be executed with the project running locally
** 🖥️ Local execution (developer machine)
** 🤖 Remote execution via Jenkins, using a dedicated environment

🎯 Goal
** 🧱 A separate environment that does not interfere with other teams
** 🗄️ A dedicated database for Gaia validation

h2. 🌙 Best Time to Run

✅ The project can be run at any time

🌙 Prefer night time / off-hours for better performance

🟢 Machines are not turned off, so overnight execution is allowed

h2. 🚀 After Every Release — Mandatory Checklist ✅

🔁 Update local project to the new release version

⬇️ Run git pull to fetch latest changes

🧹 Perform a cache clean to avoid stale artifacts

h2. 🧩 Manual Validation Scope (Before Automation)

✅ Manually validated flows
** ⚙️ Settings
** ✅ Correction

📍 Base: B2CM

🤖 Automation should start from this validated baseline

h1. 🛠️ Local Machine Setup

h2. ✅ Step 1 — Clone the Projects (Web + Backend)

📥 Clone both repositories
** 🌐 Web (Front)
** 🧱 Backend (Back)

h2. ✅ Step 2 — Use the Master Branch

📌 Ensure both projects are on master

{code:bash}
git checkout master
git pull
{code}

h2. ✅ Step 3 — Install ZIP with node_modules

📦 Use the provided ZIP containing all node_modules

🎯 Purpose
** 🚀 Faster setup
** ✅ Standardized dependencies across the team

h1. 🌐 Frontend Setup (Front)

h2. ✅ Step 1 — Place .npmrc in the User Root

📌 Copy .npmrc to:
** C:\Users<YOUR_USER>.npmrc

h2. ✅ Step 2 — Install Dependencies

📂 Open a terminal inside the frontend project folder and run:

{code:bash}
npm i
{code}

h2. ✅ Step 3 — Update Credentials in .npmrc

🔐 Open .npmrc and update:
** User and Password with your own

🧩 Also update the text below the second user/password to:
** ✍️ <PLACE_PHRASE_HERE>

{panel:title=Security Note ⚠️|borderStyle=solid|borderColor=#d04437|titleBGColor=#ffecec|bgColor=#ffffff}
Treat .npmrc as sensitive. Avoid committing it and avoid sharing screenshots with credentials.
{panel}

h2. ✅ Step 4 — Start the Frontend
{code:bash}
npm start
{code}

h1. 🧱 Backend Setup (Back)

h2. ✅ Step 1 — Edit application.properties

📂 File location:
** src/main/resources/application.properties

🔎 Find the comment section:
** #starburst datasource

🧷 In the second paragraph (middle) of that comment block, add:

{code:properties}
spring.datasource.portal.password=b2c
spring.datasource.b2c.password=b2c
spring.datasource.ctrlm.password=HEv4Tche
spring.datasource.uliss.password=YE8i26572u
spring.datasource.starburst.password=$%77eS#IhdGfmePndv[7=
{code}

{panel:title=Security Note ⚠️|borderStyle=solid|borderColor=#d04437|titleBGColor=#ffecec|bgColor=#ffffff}
These are credentials. Keep them protected, do not expose in commits, and avoid printing them in logs.
{panel}

h2. ✅ Step 2 — Run the Backend

📂 In the backend project folder, run:

{code:bash}
mvn clean spring-boot:run
{code}

h1. ▶️ Recommended Run Order

1️⃣ Start Backend first

2️⃣ Start Frontend second

3️⃣ 🧪 Run Gaia tests only after both are healthy

h1. ✅ Quick Health Check

🟢 Backend terminal shows application started without errors

🟢 Frontend opens and loads pages successfully

🧪 Only then execute the Gaia test suite
